reg_decoder_fld_t mau_match_merge_addrmap__predication_ctl_fld_list[] = {
    { "table_thread", 15, 0, 0,0, 
      "16 bits for 16 logical tables. Each bit says the table belongs in that thread. There is an array of 2 of these registers, The array index is for thread: 0 = ingress, 1 = egress. So each 16b vector says which tables belong to  its thread, ingress for the ingress array element  and egress for the egress array element." },
    { "start_table_fifo_delay0", 20, 16, 0,0, 
      "When start_table fifo0 is enabled, specifies the delay of this fifo. This should be set to the number of clock cycles of delay between the stages minus 1. For match dependency, this is given by: MAUprev(length) - MAUprev(predication cycle) + MAU(predication cycle) - 1 For action depenency, this simplifies to 1. For concurrent, this FIFO is disabled (bypassed). For the first stage, this simplifies to: MAU(predication cycle) - 1" },
    { "start_table_fifo_delay1", 25, 21, 0,0, 
      "When start_table fifo1 is enabled, specifies the delay of this fifo. This output is used to enable or clock-gate match RAMs and TCAMs if the start-table address is beyond them. This is programmed using the following equation, where the MAUprev is the PREVIOUS stage: MAUprev(length) - MAUprev(predication cycle)" },
    { "start_table_fifo_enable", 27, 26, 0,0, 
      "Enable control for the two predication FIFOs delaying start_table input. Bit 0 enables start_table_fifo_delay0, which is used to delay start_table until this stage's predication cycle. Bit 0 is enabled if this stage is match dependent or action dependent on the previous stage or is the first stage. Disable Bit 0 if this stage is concurrent with the previous stage. Bit 1 enables start_table_fifo_delay1, which is used to delay start_table for TCAM/SRAM power savings. This power saving is only available if this stage is match dependent on the previous stage. It is not available in MAU Stage 0. Don't enable Bit 1 in any other dependency case." },
};
